{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791339975247,"sessionID":"ses_eebd2826affeACkZSg43c3MZBb","part":{"id":"prt_1142ed233001STz66y4NUWdTYV","messageID":"msg_1142ec927001xY8SKBMZ4DEQfb","sessionID":"ses_eebd2826affeACkZSg43c3MZBb","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791339975302,"sessionID":"ses_eebd2826affeACkZSg43c3MZBb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"37JNWgywtdQsPQid","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"filePath":"/home/user/auto-psych/docs/auto_rsa/SMOKE_RESULTS.md"},"output":"<path>/home/user/auto-psych/docs/auto_rsa/SMOKE_RESULTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # RSA loop smoke test with real Gemini agents: results\n2: \n3: Run 2026-10-06 23:14 to 2026-10-07 00:11 UTC (56 min), in a disposable\n4: claude.ai cloud container (4 CPUs), on branch `auto-rsa-smoke` (from\n5: `auto-rsa` at `c1dd78f`), following `HANDOFF_smoke_test.md`:\n6: \n7: ```bash\n8: uv run python -m src.rsa.loop.run --results data/rsa/loop_smoke \\\n9:     --max-iterations 1 --candidate-count 3 --no-sandbox \\\n10:     --num-warmup 500 --num-samples 500 --num-chains 2\n11: ```\n12: \n13: Agents: opencode 1.18.35, `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (the default).\n14: Data: all 6,703 included forced-choice pragmods trials. Run outputs that are\n15: small are committed under `data/rsa/loop_smoke/` (report, history, ledger,\n16: each candidate's files and agent logs; not `.fit_cache/`, `responses.csv`\n17: or opencode's `.xdg_data/` snapshots).\n18: \n19: ## Verdict\n20: \n21: **Success on the handoff's criterion. The self-check did not work in this run,\n22: and the repair path was never exercised.**\n23: \n24: - Two of three slots wrote a memo model that passed every gate (code, contract,\n25:   fit, convergence, finite ELPD, novelty) on the **first** attempt. One of\n26:   them, `rsa_l2_salience`, is the new best model: −4955.5, which is\n27:   17.7 ± 2.7 nats ahead of the previous best seed `rsa_l1_salience`.\n28: - Neither agent ever saw a self-check result. Every self-check call failed: on\n29:   a CLI bug (now fixed) or on opencode's 120 s shell timeout (fixed in the\n30:   brief and primer). Their models passed because they stayed close to the\n31:   seed files' memo, not because the self-check caught anything.\n32: - One slot (refine incumbent) wrote no `candidate.py`, twice. No candidate was\n33:   rejected, so **no repair ran**. Whether the rejection reasons let a repair\n34:   succeed is still untested.\n35: - The agents hit **no memo errors at all**. Each one read seed files first and\n36:   changed them in small steps (a new prior, an extra level). The primer's\n37:   gotchas were not tested in anger.\n38: \n39: ## Per slot\n40: \n41: | Slot | Role | Outcome | Model | ELPD-LOO | Novelty: nearest (RMSE) | Self-check | Agent wall time | Tokens (in / cached / out / reasoning) | Cost |\n42: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n43: | 1 | explore (lens: \"a genuinely different family\") | **admitted** | `literal_speaker_inverter` | −5046.1 (90.6 ± 15.3 behind) | `rsa_l1_shared_prior` (0.045) | 3 calls: usage error, then killed at 120 s twice | 12 min | 77k / 63k / 0.8k / 15.1k | $0.36 |\n44: | 2 | refine incumbent (`rsa_l1_salience`) | **no file** | (drafts in `/tmp`, never in its dir) | — | — | 1 call, killed at 120 s | 20 min (killed at the limit) | 57k / 152k / 0.9k / 2.0k | $0.18 |\n45: | 2 retry | same | **no file** | — | — | — | none | 20 min (killed at the limit) | not reported (killed) | ? |\n46: | 3 | refine chosen | **admitted** | `rsa_l2_salience` | **−4955.5 (best)** | `rsa_l1_salience` (0.010) | 3 calls: usage error, then killed at 120 s twice | 19 min | 39k / 256k / 1.1k / 3.0k | $0.18 |\n47: \n48: Reported spend: **$0.71** for the round. The killed retry reported no usage,\n49: so the true figure is a little higher. Token use per slot is small: ~33k of\n50: each prompt is the brief, primer and handbook, which caching mostly absorbs.\n51: \n52: Phase timing: seed fits 6.5 min (5 models); agents 20 min (bound by the\n53: agent timeout of slot 2); the retry 20 min (killed again); admission fits of\n54: the two candidates 4 min; scoring and report 4 min.\n55: \n56: ### Slot 1: `literal_speaker_inverter` (explore)\n57: \n58: > Listeners invert a zero-order \"literal\" speaker (S0) who simply picks one\n59: > of the object's features uniformly at random, without simulating a\n60: > listener. The pragmatic preference for simpler objects emerges entirely\n61: > from probability dilution.\n62: \n63: This is a genuinely different mechanism: L1 over a literal speaker, with no\n64: informativity term, and a prior on familiarization, grayscale and feature\n65: count. It is 90.6 nats behind the best model, yet clearly better than the\n66: literal listener. It is a useful contrast: the data favour a speaker who\n67: weighs informativity. The agent spent its first step on 15k reasoning tokens\n68: and wrote all three files in one heredoc, and its memo compiled first time.\n69: \n70: ### Slot 2: refine incumbent, no candidate (twice)\n71: \n72: The first agent read the seeds and drafted a depth-2 salience model in\n73: `/tmp/cand_l2/` and in `test_l2_salience.py` **in the repository root**. It ran\n74: the self-check on `/tmp/cand_l2`, which was killed at 120 s. It then pivoted to\n75: an L1 + grayscale-prior variant (`/tmp/cand_l1_color/`, `test_l1_color.py` in\n76: the repo root), and was killed at the 1,200 s agent limit while that check\n77: ran. It never wrote to its candidate directory.\n78: \n79: The retry agent's first event came 13 min 46 s after spawn (one `cat` of a\n80: seed file); it then went silent until the 20 min limit killed it. This looks\n81: like Gemini preview latency or a stalled request, not anything in the brief.\n82: \n83: Under bubblewrap (production) the stray files in the repo root would have\n84: failed (read-only tree), and so would the `/tmp` drafts once the sandbox was\n85: gone. Either way the slot would be empty.\n86: \n87: ### Slot 3: `rsa_l2_salience` (refine chosen)\n88: \n89: > I refine the `rsa_l2` model by giving its top-level pragmatic listener the\n90: > learned salience prior over objects (based on feature count and\n91: > familiarization) …\n92: \n93: This is a single stated change, the refinement brief's intended use: the\n94: salience prior of `rsa_l1_salience` grafted onto the top level of `rsa_l2`.\n95: It is the round's discovery. The best model now has a depth-2 listener *and*\n96: a salience prior, and leads by 17.7 nats (6.5 SE). Its novelty margin is small\n97: but clear: RMSE 0.010 from `rsa_l1_salience`, against a threshold of 0.002.\n98: Slot 2's abandoned draft was nearly the same model (the prior at every level),\n99: so the two refinement slots converged on one idea.\n100: \n101: ## Bugs found and fixed (each with a test)\n102: \n103: 1. **The documented self-check command did not parse.**\n104:    - **Cause:** The brief and primer give\n105:      `check_candidate <dir> --responses <csv>`, but the tyro CLI declared\n106:      `candidate_dir` as a required `--candidate-dir` flag.\n107:    - **Effect:** All three agents ran the documented form first and got a\n108:      usage error.\n109:    - **Fix:** `candidate_dir` is now positional\n110:      (`tyro.conf.Positional`, `src/rsa/loop/check_candidate.py`).\n111:    - **Test:** `tests/test_rsa_loop_brief.py::test_the_documented_self_check_command_parses`\n112:      parses the command exactly as `CHECK_COMMAND` writes it.\n113: 2. **The self-check never finished inside an agent.**\n114:    - **Cause:** opencode's shell tool kills a command after 120 s by default.\n115:      The self-check takes 2 min 11 s on an idle 4-CPU container, and longer\n116:      while three agents run checks at once.\n117:    - **Effect:** All five correctly formed self-check calls were killed\n118:      before printing a verdict.\n119:    - **Verified:** opencode's shell tool accepts a `timeout` parameter, and a\n120:      150 s command with `timeout: 300000` completed.\n\n(Showing lines 1-120 of 187. Use offset=121 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# RSA loop smoke test with real Gemini agents: results\n\nRun 2026-10-06 23:14 to 2026-10-07 00:11 UTC (56 min), in a disposable\nclaude.ai cloud container (4 CPUs), on branch `auto-rsa-smoke` (from\n`auto-rsa` at `c1dd78f`), following `HANDOFF_smoke_test.md`:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m src.rsa.loop.run --results data/rsa/loop_smoke \\\n    --max-iterations 1 --candidate-count 3 --no-sandbox \\\n    --num-warmup 500 --num-samples 500 --num-chains 2\n```\n\nAgents: opencode 1.18.35, `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (the default).\nData: all 6,703 included forced-choice pragmods trials. Run outputs that are\nsmall are committed under `data/rsa/loop_smoke/` (report, history, ledger,\neach candidate's files and agent logs; not `.fit_cache/`, `responses.csv`\nor opencode's `.xdg_data/` snapshots).\n\n## Verdict\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/user/auto-psych/docs/auto_rsa/SMOKE_RESULTS.md","text":"# RSA loop smoke test with real Gemini agents: results\n\nRun 2026-10-06 23:14 to 2026-10-07 00:11 UTC (56 min), in a disposable\nclaude.ai cloud container (4 CPUs), on branch `auto-rsa-smoke` (from\n`auto-rsa` at `c1dd78f`), following `HANDOFF_smoke_test.md`:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m src.rsa.loop.run --results data/rsa/loop_smoke \\\n    --max-iterations 1 --candidate-count 3 --no-sandbox \\\n    --num-warmup 500 --num-samples 500 --num-chains 2\n```\n\nAgents: opencode 1.18.35, `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (the default).\nData: all 6,703 included forced-choice pragmods trials. Run outputs that are\nsmall are committed under `data/rsa/loop_smoke/` (report, history, ledger,\neach candidate's files and agent logs; not `.fit_cache/`, `responses.csv`\nor opencode's `.xdg_data/` snapshots).\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Success on the handoff's criterion. The self-check did not work in this run,\nand the repair path was never exercised.**\n\n- Two of three slots wrote a memo model that passed every gate (code, contract,\n  fit, convergence, finite ELPD, novelty) on the **first** attempt. One of\n  them, `rsa_l2_salience`, is the new best model: −4955.5, which is\n  17.7 ± 2.7 nats ahead of the previous best seed `rsa_l1_salience`.\n- Neither agent ever saw a self-check result. Every self-check call failed: on\n  a CLI bug (now fixed) or on opencode's 120 s shell timeout (fixed in the\n  brief and primer). Their models passed because they stayed close to the\n  seed files' memo, not because the self-check caught anything.\n- One slot (refine incumbent) wrote no `candidate.py`, twice. No candidate was\n  rejected, so **no repair ran**. Whether the rejection reasons let a repair\n  succeed is still untested.\n- The agents hit **no memo errors at all**. Each one read seed files first and\n  changed them in small steps (a new prior, an extra level). The primer's\n  gotchas were not tested in anger.\n\n## Per slot\n\n| Slot | Role | Outcome | Model | ELPD-LOO | Novelty: nearest (RMSE) | Self-check | Agent wall time | Tokens (in / cached / out / reasoning) | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | explore (lens: \"a genuinely different family\") | **admitted** | `literal_speaker_inverter` | −5046.1 (90.6 ± 15.3 behind) | `rsa_l1_shared_prior` (0.045) | 3 calls: usage error, then killed at 120 s twice | 12 min | 77k / 63k / 0.8k / 15.1k | $0.36 |\n| 2 | refine incumbent (`rsa_l1_salience`) | **no file** | (drafts in `/tmp`, never in its dir) | — | — | 1 call, killed at 120 s | 20 min (killed at the limit) | 57k / 152k / 0.9k / 2.0k | $0.18 |\n| 2 retry | same | **no file** | — | — | — | none | 20 min (killed at the limit) | not reported (killed) | ? |\n| 3 | refine chosen | **admitted** | `rsa_l2_salience` | **−4955.5 (best)** | `rsa_l1_salience` (0.010) | 3 calls: usage error, then killed at 120 s twice | 19 min | 39k / 256k / 1.1k / 3.0k | $0.18 |\n\nReported spend: **$0.71** for the round. The killed retry reported no usage,\nso the true figure is a little higher. Token use per slot is small: ~33k of\neach prompt is the brief, primer and handbook, which caching mostly absorbs.\n\nPhase timing: seed fits 6.5 min (5 models); agents 20 min (bound by the\nagent timeout of slot 2); the retry 20 min (killed again); admission fits of\nthe two candidates 4 min; scoring and report 4 min.\n\n### Slot 1: `literal_speaker_inverter` (explore)\n\n> Listeners invert a zero-order \"literal\" speaker (S0) who simply picks one\n> of the object's features uniformly at random, without simulating a\n> listener. The pragmatic preference for simpler objects emerges entirely\n> from probability dilution.\n\nThis is a genuinely different mechanism: L1 over a literal speaker, with no\ninformativity term, and a prior on familiarization, grayscale and feature\ncount. It is 90.6 nats behind the best model, yet clearly better than the\nliteral listener. It is a useful contrast: the data favour a speaker who\nweighs informativity. The agent spent its first step on 15k reasoning tokens\nand wrote all three files in one heredoc, and its memo compiled first time.\n\n### Slot 2: refine incumbent, no candidate (twice)\n\nThe first agent read the seeds and drafted a depth-2 salience model in\n`/tmp/cand_l2/` and in `test_l2_salience.py` **in the repository root**. It ran\nthe self-check on `/tmp/cand_l2`, which was killed at 120 s. It then pivoted to\nan L1 + grayscale-prior variant (`/tmp/cand_l1_color/`, `test_l1_color.py` in\nthe repo root), and was killed at the 1,200 s agent limit while that check\nran. It never wrote to its candidate directory.\n\nThe retry agent's first event came 13 min 46 s after spawn (one `cat` of a\nseed file); it then went silent until the 20 min limit killed it. This looks\nlike Gemini preview latency or a stalled request, not anything in the brief.\n\nUnder bubblewrap (production) the stray files in the repo root would have\nfailed (read-only tree), and so would the `/tmp` drafts once the sandbox was\ngone. Either way the slot would be empty.\n\n### Slot 3: `rsa_l2_salience` (refine chosen)\n\n> I refine the `rsa_l2` model by giving its top-level pragmatic listener the\n> learned salience prior over objects (based on feature count and\n> familiarization) …\n\nThis is a single stated change, the refinement brief's intended use: the\nsalience prior of `rsa_l1_salience` grafted onto the top level of `rsa_l2`.\nIt is the round's discovery. The best model now has a depth-2 listener *and*\na salience prior, and leads by 17.7 nats (6.5 SE). Its novelty margin is small\nbut clear: RMSE 0.010 from `rsa_l1_salience`, against a threshold of 0.002.\nSlot 2's abandoned draft was nearly the same model (the prior at every level),\nso the two refinement slots converged on one idea.\n\n## Bugs found and fixed (each with a test)\n\n1. **The documented self-check command did not parse.**\n   - **Cause:** The brief and primer give\n     `check_candidate <dir> --responses <csv>`, but the tyro CLI declared\n     `candidate_dir` as a required `--candidate-dir` flag.\n   - **Effect:** All three agents ran the documented form first and got a\n     usage error.\n   - **Fix:** `candidate_dir` is now positional\n     (`tyro.conf.Positional`, `src/rsa/loop/check_candidate.py`).\n   - **Test:** `tests/test_rsa_loop_brief.py::test_the_documented_self_check_command_parses`\n     parses the command exactly as `CHECK_COMMAND` writes it.\n2. **The self-check never finished inside an agent.**\n   - **Cause:** opencode's shell tool kills a command after 120 s by default.\n     The self-check takes 2 min 11 s on an idle 4-CPU container, and longer\n     while three agents run checks at once.\n   - **Effect:** All five correctly formed self-check calls were killed\n     before printing a verdict.\n   - **Verified:** opencode's shell tool accepts a `timeout` parameter, and a\n     150 s command with `timeout: 300000` completed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":120,"totalLines":187,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/auto_rsa/SMOKE_RESULTS.md","time":{"start":1791339975238,"end":1791339975260}},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"id":"prt_1142ed23a001X6OhNwjnEkL4to","sessionID":"ses_eebd2826affeACkZSg43c3MZBb","messageID":"msg_1142ec927001xY8SKBMZ4DEQfb"}}
